    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.mmuplink.tooltip=Machine Type: §eMatter Manipulator Quantum Uplink§r\nInterdimensional and infinite range uplink for matter manipulators.\nAllows manipulators to convert plans into AE patterns.\nConnects directly to an ME system via a §6Quantum Uplink ME Connector Hatch§7.\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nConsumes 1A ZPM while active.\nMust be fed with plasma via an input hatch.\nTransfers to/from the manipulator cost 131,072 EU in plasma per item or per bucket.\nInsert a compatible manipulator in the controller slot while the machine is running to bind it to the uplink.\n§aSupports Multi-Amp and Laser Hatches!\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.mmuplink.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §69§7x§69§7x§69§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center, 5th layer\n   §60-121 §fAdvanced Iridium Plated Machine Casing\n   §624 §fMatter Generation Coil\n   §620 §fTrinium Frame Box\n   §64 §fNaquadah Alloy Frame Box\n   §62 §fRadiant Naquadah Alloy Casing\n   §e0-1 §fQuantum Uplink ME Connector Hatch: §7Any iridium casing\n   §e1+ §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any iridium casing\n   §e1+ §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any iridium casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any iridium casing\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.nanochipassemblycomplex.tooltip=Machine Type: §eNAC, Nanochip Assembly Complex§r\nUses Circuit Components (§eCCs§7) to create circuits at unimaginable speeds\nClick the Logo Icon in the GUI for more information\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§eCCs§7 can only exist in the perfect environment present in §fVacuum Conveyor Hatches§7\nConvert items to §eCCs§7 in the control room by placing them in a §cc§eo§al§3o§br§de§5d§7 input bus\nEvery §45§7 seconds, all items in §cc§eo§al§3o§br§de§5d§7 input buses are placed\nin Vacuum Conveyor Outputs (§eVCOs§7) of the same §cc§eo§al§bo§dr§7\nFinished circuit §eCCs§7 are converted back into circuits by routing them to a §eVCI§7 in the control room\n§eCCs§7 in a §cc§eo§al§3o§br§de§5d§7 §eVCI§7 are placed in an output bus of the same §cc§eo§al§bo§dr§7\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§eCCs§7 must be processed into a refined version by §f§nmodules§r§7 before they\ncan be assembled into a circuit in the §aNanochip Assembly Matrix\nAll power from the energy hatch is distributed to the modules as they need it\n§aSupports Multi-Amp and Laser Hatches!\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§d§oHome of the Gestalt Rapidly Evolving Genesis Optimization System (GREGOS),§7\n§d§oa pseudo-sentient program overseeing circuit production in the NAC§7\n§d§oIt seems to be eager to learn more, maybe you can become friends?§7\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.nanochipassemblycomplex.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §663§7x§663§7x§649§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Middle of structure, 9th layer\n   §63958 §fNanochip Reinforcement Casing\n   §62226 §fNanochip Complex Glass\n   §61124-1719 §fNanochip Mesh Interface Casing\n   §6721 §fNanochip Computational Matrix Casing\n   §653 §fNaquadah Frame Box\n   §632 §fNanochip Firewall Projection Casing\n   §e0-12 §fNAC Module: §7Any top center edge mesh casing on platform\n   §e1 §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any side mesh casing in control room\n   §e1+ §fInput Bus: §7Any side mesh casing in control room\n   §e1+ §fOutput Bus: §7Any side mesh casing in control room\n   §e0+ §fVacuum Conveyor Input: §7Any side mesh casing in control room\n   §e0+ §fVacuum Conveyor Output: §7Any side mesh casing in control room\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.nanochipmodule.assemblymatrix.tooltip=Machine Type: §eAssembly Matrix, NAC Module§r\nModule of the §aNanochip Assembly Complex§7\nAssembles your Circuits §eCCs§7 with Component §eCCs§7\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nMaximum allowed Recipe Tier is determined by §fComponent Assembly Line Casing§7 Tier\nOverclocks recipes (Energy Hatch Tier - Recipe Tier) times\n§b-5%§7 EU Usage per §fComponent Assembly Line Casing§7 Tier above the Recipe Tier (multiplicative)\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§d§oAfter processing your CCs through an intricate pipeline, they are finally§7\n§d§oready to be assembled into a circuit. This circuit can be converted into a real§7\n§d§oitem in the NAC control center, or processed further into a higher tier circuit§7\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
